// Signing for the Resoniq target, and the one per-developer setting besides it.
//
// The Apple Developer Team ID is not committed. Put it in Config/Signing.local.xcconfig (gitignored):
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = XXXXXXXXXX
//
// Without it the simulator still builds and runs; only a device build needs the team.
// Choosing the team in Xcode's Signing tab instead writes it into the generated project, which is not committed.

// Where "Share recordings for research" sends kept tests (docs/plans/phase-10-share-recordings.md). Empty here, so a
// build from the repository has no sharing at all: no Settings row, and no object that could make a request. The
// owner sets it in Config/Signing.local.xcconfig. In an xcconfig `//` starts a comment, so write the slashes with an
// empty `$()` between them:
//
//     RESONIQ_SHARE_URL = https:/$()/share.example.com
//     RESONIQ_SHARE_URL = http:/$()/localhost:8787        (a Worker run with `wrangler dev`; Debug builds only)
//
// Never commit a real URL.
RESONIQ_SHARE_URL =

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
